      "message": "This causes a slight change in the output of constants.bzl, but is (probably) necessary for Java flags because there are some arguments with nested strings which get split mid-argument.\n\nI had to make a slight change to one of the CC config options in `x86_linux_host.go` because I got this error:\n```\nclang: error: unsupported option \u0027--sysroot prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/host/x86_64-linux-glibc2.17-4.8/sysroot\u0027\n```\n\nBecause this flag is now submitted as a single string instead of two separate strings. Splitting up the flag solved this problem, but it seems strange that it caused an issue in the first place.",
